---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description={`About ${SITE.name} — background, experience, and what I'm looking for.`}
>
  <div class="wrap about">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <!-- Drafted from your CV. Read it aloud once and adjust anything that
         doesn't sound like you — it should read as a person talking, not a
         profile being recited. -->
    <p>
      I'm a software engineer based in Khmelnytskyi, Ukraine. For the past eight
      years I've built production systems end to end — the AI that makes a
      decision, the interface someone actually uses to act on it, and the data
      infrastructure feeding both. I've never found those three to be separable
      problems, and most of my work has come from being willing to own all of them.
    </p>

    <p>
      Lately that's meant RAG systems and agent workflows: retrieval that returns
      the right context, agents that behave predictably enough to ship, and the
      evaluation and human-in-the-loop validation needed to trust either one. Built
      with LangChain, LangGraph, the OpenAI Agent SDK, and vector search — though
      the hard part is rarely the framework. It's retrieval quality and the data
      underneath.
    </p>

    <p>
      That data layer is the part I've done longest: ETL and ELT pipelines,
      analytical warehouses, and real-time streaming in Python, PySpark,
      Databricks, Kafka, dbt, Airflow, and Dagster. On the other side of it I work
      in TypeScript, React, and Next.js, with Python/FastAPI and Node.js services
      behind them, deployed on AWS with Docker and Kubernetes. I care about the
      unglamorous properties — data quality, governance, and observability —
      because they decide whether a system survives contact with production.
    </p>

    <p>
      The work has spanned healthcare, fintech, and autonomous vehicles: clinical
      reasoning over medical literature and patient data, real-time trading
      infrastructure across several broker APIs, and active learning loops for
      vehicle perception models. Along the way I've mentored nine junior and
      mid-level engineers, which has reliably taught me more than it taught them.
    </p>

    <p>
      <!-- TODO: Confirm this. Your CV shows you freelancing through Toptal since
           Feb 2026, so I've written it that way — but if you're actually after a
           full-time role, or open to relocation, say so here. This is the
           sentence that turns a reader into an email. -->
      I'm currently taking on freelance and contract work through Toptal, mostly
      partnering with startups and technical leaders on AI, data, and cloud
      infrastructure. If you're building something in that space, I'd like to hear
      about it.
    </p>

    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <ul class="roles">
      <li>
        <span class="role-title">Senior Software Engineer</span>
        <span class="org">Toptal (Freelance)</span>
        <span class="dates">02/2026 — Present</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="role-title">Senior Software Engineer</span>
        <span class="org">Diana Health · Texas, United States</span>
        <span class="dates">07/2024 — 12/2025</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="role-title">Full-Stack Engineer</span>
        <span class="org">Upwork (Freelance)</span>
        <span class="dates">03/2020 — 06/2024</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="role-title">Junior Backend Developer → AI &amp; Full-Stack Engineer</span>
        <span class="org">Arc XP · Washington, United States</span>
        <span class="dates">06/2018 — 05/2020</span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Education</h2>
    <ul class="roles">
      <li>
        <span class="role-title">BEng, Computer Science</span>
        <span class="org">Sumy State University · Sumy, Ukraine</span>
        <span class="dates">2013 — 2017</span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="cv-note">
      <!-- Put your CV PDF in public/ and it'll be served at this path. -->
      Full history: <a href="/cv.pdf">download CV (PDF)</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <p>
      Reach me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .about h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .roles {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .roles li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.1rem;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .roles li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .role-title {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .org,
  .dates {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .dates {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }

  .cv-note {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
</style>
